{
  "raw": {
    "http://mcla.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205392": {
      "title": "Director of TRIO Student Support Services Program",
      "description": "Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts\nJob Posting: Director of TRIO Student Support Services Program Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts \n\tJob Posting: Director of TRIO Student Support Services Program Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director of TRIO Student Support Services Program Category: Administrative Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Academic Locations: North Adams, MA Posted: Oct 1, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 205392 Share About Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts: At MCLA, we're here for all, and focused on each of our students. Classes are taught by educators who care deeply about teaching, and about seeing their students thrive on every level of their lives. In every way possible, the experience at MCLA is designed to elevate our students as individuals, leaders, and communicators, fully empowered to make their impressions on the world. In addition to our 132-year commitment to public education, we have fortified our dedication to equitable academic excellence. MCLA has appeared on U.S. News & World Report's list of Top Ten Public Colleges for 11 consecutive years, earning the No. 6 spot on the list of Top Public Liberal Arts Schools in the nation for 2026. The College's focus on affordable education and economic prosperity is reflected in additional 2026 U.S. News rankings: No. 6 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for liberal arts colleges in the state and No. 4 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for public liberal arts colleges in the country. These rankings measure how well schools graduate students who receive Federal Pell Grants. Learn more at www.mcla.edu Job Description: GENERAL STATEMENT OF DUTIES: The Program Director for the TRIO Student Support Services Program (SSS) oversees a U.S. Department of Education grant-funded program providing comprehensive academic and holistic services to college students to support their academic, social, personal development, and well-being needs. Students served by TRIO SSS are first generation, come from a low-income background, and/or have a disability. The Project Director will lead the development, implementation, administration, assessment, staffing, models, and activities of the program in accordance with federal regulations, grant objectives, and MCLA strategic priorities. The Program Director helps advance an institution-wide collaborative model for TRIO SSS. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: Reports to the Dean of the Library and Integrated Student Support SUPERVISION EXERCISED: Supervises TRIO program staff and student employees DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Oversee the strategic planning, administration, assessment, reporting, and implementation of the TRIO SSS grant in accordance with USDOE TRIO SSS rules and regulations and in alignment with MCLA priorities. Manage the program budget and authorize expenditures of federal funds in collaboration with involved departments and offices. Complete and submit the project's Annual Performance Report (APR) in accordance with USDOE instructions and with support from MCLA collaborators including Institutional Research, Grants staff, and TRIO SSS program staff,. Collaboratively develop and implement a recruitment and persistence plan for TRIO students; assure equal access to project services for all project participants; develop and scaffold tiered engagement and intervention strategies and activities that are universal and customized in design, as well as impactful in closing equity gaps. Supervise the selection/eligibility of TRIO SSS program participants according to SSS guidelines; collect and maintain program data and prepare reports as required by the USDOE and MCLA. Recruit, hire, train, supervise, professionally support, and evaluate TRIO project staff and student employees. Allocate advising and engagement caseloads among the director and project staff. Provide academic coaching, encouragement, and support to 160+ program participants. Apply principles of appreciative advising and active learning to build rapport, engagement and trust with students. Help students design and implement academic success plans that include goals and objectives and address areas of need. Support successful goal completion and monitor student progress toward established goals. May serve on the MCLA CARE/case management team and/or the Academic Appeals Committee Plan and facilitate program-sponsored events in collaboration with TRIO SSS project staff and campus partners. Coordinate with Student Affairs on activities for first-generation students. Establish and maintain liaison relationships and collaborations with offices and units across divisions to facilitate referrals, awareness, and collaboration. Lead and participate in committees and work groups that align with project goals and objectives. Participate in college-wide initiatives and signature events. Coordinate public relations initiatives for TRIO SSS; foster an institutional climate in support of the project's mission, goals, and objectives; promote an inclusive culture and community. Disseminate USDOE and TRIO SSS-related information to broaden familiarity with TRIO SSS. Serve as the university representative for TRIO with the US Department of Education. Perform other duties as assigned. Requirements: MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Master's degree in relevant field (Education, Behavioral and/or Social Science, Higher Education Administration, Student Affairs Administration). A minimum of three years of successful program administrative and supervisory experience at the post-secondary level. Proven strategic organizational, assessment and management skills, as well as the ability to engage in effective collaborations and conflict resolution. Budget management experience required. Experience developing and implementing academic and holistic support services for student populations who are traditionally underserved in higher education, especially those who are first generation, come from a low-income background, and/or have a disability. Previous experience working with students from diverse socioeconomic and ethnic backgrounds; experience fostering inclusive communities. Prior experience in academic advising and mentoring of undergraduate students. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Previous work within a federal or state grant funded educational program and experience in writing proposals, designing, managing or implementing a TRIO SSS Program (or a similar program) preferred. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES: Knowledge of theories and best practices in student development, academic learning and well-being. Demonstrated ability to establish and maintain a productive working relationship with multiple constituencies across campus. Experience convening committees. Knowledge of college/university processes and procedures Ability to work with and safeguard sensitive and confidential student information. Working knowledge of student management database systems and learning platforms, such as EAB Navigate360, Canvas, BANNER and DegreeWorks. Well-developed written and oral communication skills, including developing and delivering presentations. Additional Information: This is a full-time position within the APA bargaining union. This position is grant-funded through August 31, 2030. Continuation of the position is dependent on renewal of the grant. Salary for this position is $75,000-$80,000 per year. Employee Benefits: Health Insurance: MCLA offers a variety of HMO, POS, and PPO-type health insurance plans for eligible employees. Coverage is effective on the 1st of the month following the date of hire. Exceptions to employees hired on the 1st of the month, coverage is effective immediately. Retirement: The MA State Employee Retirement System provides eligible employees with a retirement pension following a 10-year vesting period. In lieu of the retirement pension, eligible employees may select the Optional Retirement Plan with a maximum 5% employer matching contribution. Tuition Waivers & Discounts: eligible employees, including spouses and dependent children, receive reduced tuition at MA state colleges, community colleges, and universities. Paid Time Off: employees receive 12 paid holidays and generous vacation, personal, and sick leave benefits. Until further notice, in response to the Presidential proclamation, issued on September 19, 2025, imposing a significant fee on the entry of individuals with new H-1B visas, this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. Should you need to request a reasonable accommodation for the application process, please email Brenda Stokes, Executive Director of Human Resources. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts is deeply committed to fostering a community of excellence, equity, diversity, and inclusion. We provide equal access to educational, co-curricular and employment opportunities for all applicants, students, and employees regardless of race, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, marital or parental status, veteran status, or membership in any other legally protected class. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any educational program or activity that they operate, which extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about Title IX, Equal Opportunity, or ADA/504 and other non-discrimination policies may be directed to MCLA's Interim Title IX and Equal Opportunity Coordinator, to the Assistant Secretary of the Department of Education Office for Civil Rights, or both. Lucas Morrill Interim Title IX and EO Coordinator 375 Church Street, North Adams, MA 01247 Telephone: (413) 662-5103 Titleix@mcla.edu U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights 33 Arch Street, 9th Floor Boston, MA 02119-1424 Telephone: (617) 289-0111; FAX: (617) 289-0150; TDD (877) 521-2172 OCR.Boston@ed.gov Application Instructions: Applicants are required to submit a resume, cover letter, online application and 3 professional references. Candidates should electronically submit an application materials by clicking on the APPLY NOW button below. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Massachusetts college of liberal Arts - Main Campus 375 Church Street North Adams, MA 01247"
    },
    "http://mcla.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205068": {
      "title": "Government Relations Officer",
      "description": "Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts\nJob Posting: Government Relations Officer Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts \n\tJob Posting: Government Relations Officer Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Government Relations Officer Category: Administrative Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Administrative &nbsp; Locations: North Adams, MA Posted: Sep 22, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 205068 Share About Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts: At MCLA, we're here for all and focused on each of our students. Classes are taught by educators who care deeply about teaching, and about seeing their students thrive on every level of their lives. In every way possible, the experience at MCLA is designed to elevate our students as individuals, leaders, and communicators, fully empowered to make their impressions on the world. In addition to our 132-year commitment to public education, we have fortified our dedication to equitable academic excellence. MCLA has appeared on U.S. News & World Report's list of Top Ten Public Colleges for 11 consecutive years, earning the No. 6 spot on the list of Top Public Liberal Arts Schools in the nation for 2026. The College's focus on affordable education and economic prosperity is reflected in additional 2026 U.S. News rankings: No. 6 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for liberal arts colleges in the state and No. 4 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for public liberal arts colleges in the country. These rankings measure how well schools graduate students who receive Federal Pell Grants. Learn more at www.mcla.edu Job Description: GENERAL STATEMENT OF DUTIES: The Government Relations Officer is responsible for the management and coordination of the Colleges' political relationships with state and federal government entities.  Serving as the College's primary contact for government matters, the officer pursues public-sector opportunities while collaborating with government stakeholders. The Officer will cultivate and maintain effective relationships with elected officials, government agencies, funding partners, and policymakers to advance the Colleges' strategic priorities and institutional interests. The Officer will work closely with the College's leadership team to constantly assess, refine, and adjust a government relations strategy and will then leverage partnerships to progress the institution forward. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: President SUPERVISION EXERCISED: None DETAILED STATEMENT OF DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Manage the College's Government Relations efforts: Responsible for managing a wide range of complex and politically sensitive legislative, funding, and issue-oriented interactions as well as campus initiatives designed to advance the mission and priorities of the campus. Leads the development of strategy and tactics to enhance state support for the institution. Draft public testimony letters or other official correspondence to elected officials, governmental agencies, rulemaking bodies, and boards. Cultivate and maintain relationships with MA legislative and executive branch officials, as well as with other MA state institutions of higher education and other related groups. Work with the Office of the Governor regarding recommendations for the Council of Trustees. Disseminate relevant information and data to bolster support for various programs and initiatives of interest and benefit to the College and the Commonwealth. In collaboration with senior campus leadership, this position shares responsibility for elevating the visibility and public funding for the campus. Monitors and evaluates legislation and regulations impacting the college, creating policy recommendations with the President's Cabinet. Act as MCLA's primary contact for major capital project funding with state agencies such as DCAMM, to ensure compliance with proposal processes and heighten MCLA's visibility with those organizations. Works diligently and creatively to find government funding sources for College's strategic initiatives. Establishes overall strategy for advocacy programs, creating and leveraging partnerships and collaboration opportunities on behalf of the College. Requires a significant presence in Boston throughout the calendar year. Monitors and evaluates legislation and regulations impacting the college, creating policy recommendations with Cabinet. Requirements: Bachelor's degree required, Master's degree in related field preferred Higher education experience is desirable A minimum 5 + years of government engagement experience Demonstrated relationship building with government officials both state and federal Excellent writing, interpersonal, and organizational skills Ability to quickly react to resource development opportunities in a rapidly changing environment to meet the needs of shifting priorities Demonstrated skill in tracking projects from initial identification through conclusion of project or to sustainability Demonstrated effectiveness in working with diverse colleagues, constituents, and stakeholders Strong technological skills, including proficiency in common Microsoft Office programs, database use, and research tools Ability to work occasional nights and weekends, and to travel regionally and nationally to accomplish the goals of the position Additional Information: This is a part-time, permanent benefited position, working 20 hours per week. This position has the option for a hybrid work schedule. Salary for this position is $50,000-$55,000 per year. Position starts on 12/01/2026. Employee Benefits: Health Insurance: MCLA offers a variety of HMO, POS, and PPO-type health insurance plans for eligible employees. Coverage is effective on the 1st of the month following the date of hire. Exceptions to employees hired on the 1st of the month, coverage is effective immediately. Retirement: The MA State Employee Retirement System provides eligible employees with a retirement pension following a 10-year vesting period. In lieu of the retirement pension, eligible employees may select the Optional Retirement Plan with a maximum 5% employer matching contribution. Tuition Waivers & Discounts: eligible employees, including spouses and dependent children, receive reduced tuition at MA state colleges, community colleges, and universities. Paid Time Off: employees receive 12 paid holidays and generous vacation, personal, and sick leave benefits. Until further notice, in response to the Presidential proclamation, issued on September 19, 2025, imposing a significant fee on the entry of individuals with new H-1B visas, this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. Should you need to request a reasonable accommodation for the application process, please email Brenda Stokes, Executive Director of Human Resources. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts is deeply committed to fostering a community of excellence, equity, diversity, and inclusion. We provide equal access to educational, co-curricular and employment opportunities for all applicants, students, and employees regardless of race, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, marital or parental status, veteran status, or membership in any other legally protected class. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any educational program or activity that they operate, which extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about Title IX, Equal Opportunity, or ADA/504 and other non-discrimination policies may be directed to MCLA's Interim Title IX and Equal Opportunity Coordinator, to the Assistant Secretary of the Department of Education Office for Civil Rights, or both. Lucas Morrill Interim Title IX and EO Coordinator 375 Church Street, North Adams, MA 01247 Telephone: (413) 662-5103 Titleix@mcla.edu U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights 33 Arch Street, 9th Floor Boston, MA 02119-1424 Telephone: (617) 289-0111; FAX: (617) 289-0150; TDD (877) 521-2172 OCR.Boston@ed.gov Application Instructions: Applicants are required to submit a resume, cover letter, online application, and 3 professional references to be considered for this position. Candidates should click the apply now button to submit application materials. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Massachusetts college of liberal Arts - Main Campus 375 Church Street North Adams, MA 01247"
    },
    "http://mcla.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204854": {
      "title": "Vice President of Administration and Finance",
      "description": "Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts\nJob Posting: Vice President of Administration and Finance Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts \n\tJob Posting: Vice President of Administration and Finance Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Vice President of Administration and Finance Category: Administrative Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: North Adams, MA Posted: Sep 16, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $235,000.00 - $250,000.00 Position ID: 204854 Share About Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts: At MCLA, we're here for all, and focused on each of our students. Classes are taught by educators who care deeply about teaching, and about seeing their students thrive on every level of their lives. In every way possible, the experience at MCLA is designed to elevate our students as individuals, leaders, and communicators, fully empowered to make their impressions on the world. In addition to our 130-year commitment to public education, we have fortified our dedication to equitable academic excellence. MCLA has appeared on U.S. News & World Report's list of Top Ten Public Colleges for 11 consecutive years, earning the No. 6 spot on the list of Top Public Liberal Arts Schools in the nation for 2026. The College's focus on affordable education and economic prosperity is reflected in additional 2026 U.S. News rankings: No. 6 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for liberal arts colleges in the state and No. 4 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for public liberal arts colleges in the country. These rankings measure how well schools graduate students who receive Federal Pell Grants. Learn more at www.mcla.edu Job Description: GENERAL STATEMENT OF DUTIES: The Vice President of Administration and Finance provides executive leadership of financial and administrative operations of the college. Primary responsibilities include providing leadership to administrative services at the college, leading development and management of the budget, allocation of fiscal resources, and implementation of elements of fiscal accountability to accomplish the college's mission. Develop and provide innovative solutions to institutional challenges through continuous assessment and improvement of operations. Serves as the chief financial officer for the college and is a member of the President's Executive Staff. The Vice President spearheads alignment of financial operations, business support functions, physical plant management and auxiliary services with strategic planning objectives. Provides management and direction to the departments of Information Technology, Facilities, Fiscal Affairs (Budgeting, Accounting, Purchasing), Shipping/Receiving and Mailroom/Copying, Capital Planning, Auxiliary Services, Risk Management, Emergency Planning, Human Resources and Student Financial Services. SUPERVISION RECEIVED : Reports directly to the President. SUPERVISION EXERCISED : Exercises supervision over professional and classified staff assigned to the Administration & Finance Division. DETAILED STATEMENT OF DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Develop, implement and enforce policies and procedures through financial and administrative systems that will improve the overall operation and effectiveness of the college. Partners with public safety leadership and other campus stakeholders to ensure effective emergency management planning, compliance, training and response coordination. Plan, develop, organize, implement, direct, and evaluate the organization's fiscal functions. Ensure timely and accurate budget analysis and financial reporting for the management team, President, and Board of Trustees. Ensure continual review and improvement of the budgeting process through education of management on financial issues impacting their budgets. Responsible for the planning, preparation, supervision, and presentation of the college's annual budget to the President and Board of Trustees, and the constituents of the college. Responsible for disseminating information within the college on budgetary processes and procedures related to operating and capital expenditures. Advise the President and management team on the impact of long range financial and organizational planning. Provide strategic financial leadership and support on potential alliances, investments and other issues affecting the college's business. Participate in the negotiation of union contracts. Provide leadership and guidance regarding the development and implementation of capital planning and operations projects as well as the safe maintenance of physical plant and grounds. Provide leadership and guidance to ensure the campus-wide technology strategy is responsive to the needs of the college community. Provide leadership and guidance to ensure effective and efficient function of the Human Resources and Payroll Department is being followed in accordance with state and federal guidelines. Establishes credibility throughout the organization and with the Board as an effective problem solver. Evaluates the finance/administrative services structure and team plan for continual improvement of the efficiency and effectiveness of the department as well as providing professional development opportunities. Collaborate with internal departments and external agents and constituencies to provide financial information/reports and to work toward the realization of cost efficiencies in line with the college's goals and strategic plan.  Assist the President in aligning strategic priorities with Massachusetts Department of Higher Education strategic initiatives. Responsible for the accounting of all funds collected from all sources of the college and the dispersal of such funds under the applicable laws and regulation of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts. Provides leadership and guidance to ensure effective and efficient function of Student Financial Services, including financial aid administration, student accounts, billing, collections, and customer service operations following all federal, state, and institutional regulations governing student financial assistance programs, including Title IV financial aid requirements. Oversee the management and monitoring of the College's investments and reserve funds in accordance with the Investment Policy approved by the Board of Trustees. Develop policies, procedures and engages in the procurement of goods and non-personnel services. Other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the President. Requirements: REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor's degree in finance or related field required. Master's degree preferred Certified Public Accountant or Certified Management Accountant preferred Experience in public higher education fiscal management An experienced leader and financial executive with at least seven years of full-time progressively responsible management experience related to administrative and fiscal affairs in a complex organization Demonstrated understanding of the importance of diversity of staff and ability to work collaboratively with a diverse faculty, staff, and student body Extensive experience with budget development and management, business accounting, risk management, contract/procurement A strategic thinker with sound technical skills, analytical ability, and strong operations and systems focus Demonstrated ability to utilize data and identify risks to analyze strategic issues and inform decisions Outstanding communication skills; a team player who can relate to a variety of constituencies.  Able to explain complex financial information in understandable terms Prior administrative experience in a collective bargaining environment preferred Additional Information: This is a full-time, permanent, benefited position starting on 1/01/2027. Salary for this position is between $235,000 and $250,000 per year. Applications received by 10/28/2026 will receive preferential treatment. Employee Benefits: Health Insurance: MCLA offers a variety of HMO, POS, and PPO-type health insurance plans for eligible employees. Coverage is effective on the 1st of the month following the date of hire. Exceptions to employees hired on the 1st of the month, coverage is effective immediately. Retirement: The MA State Employee Retirement System provides eligible employees with a retirement pension following a 10-year vesting period. In lieu of the retirement pension, eligible employees may select the Optional Retirement Plan with a maximum 5% employer matching contribution. Tuition Waivers & Discounts: eligible employees, including spouses and dependent children, receive reduced tuition at MA state colleges, community colleges, and universities. Paid Time Off: employees receive 12 paid holidays and generous vacation, personal, and sick leave benefits. Until further notice, in response to the Presidential proclamation, issued on September 19, 2025, imposing a significant fee on the entry of individuals with new H-1B visas, this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. Should you need to request a reasonable accommodation for the application process, please email Brenda Stokes, Executive Director of Human Resources. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts is deeply committed to fostering a community of excellence, equity, diversity, and inclusion. We provide equal access to educational, co-curricular and employment opportunities for all applicants, students, and employees regardless of race, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, marital or parental status, veteran status, or membership in any other legally protected class. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any educational program or activity that they operate, which extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about Title IX, Equal Opportunity, or ADA/504 and other non-discrimination policies may be directed to MCLA's Interim Title IX and Equal Opportunity Coordinator, to the Assistant Secretary of the Department of Education Office for Civil Rights, or both. Lucas Morrill Interim Title IX and EO Coordinator 375 Church Street, North Adams, MA 01247 Telephone: (413) 662-5103 Titleix@mcla.edu U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights 33 Arch Street, 9th Floor Boston, MA 02119-1424 Telephone: (617) 289-0111; FAX: (617) 289-0150; TDD (877) 521-2172 OCR.Boston@ed.gov Application Instructions: Applicants are required to submit a resume, cover letter, online application, and 3 professional references to be considered for this position. Candidates should click the apply now button to submit application materials. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Massachusetts college of liberal Arts - Main Campus 375 Church Street North Adams, MA 01247"
    },
    "http://mcla.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204637": {
      "title": "Second Shift Facilities Manager",
      "description": "Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts\nJob Posting: Second Shift Facilities Manager Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts \n\tJob Posting: Second Shift Facilities Manager Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Second Shift Facilities Manager Category: Administrative Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities Management Locations: North Adams, MA Posted: Sep 9, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204637 Share About Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts: At MCLA, we're here for all, and focused on each, of our students. Classes are taught by educators who care deeply about teaching, and about seeing their students thrive on every level of their lives. In every way possible, the experience at MCLA is designed to elevate our students as individuals, leaders, and communicators, fully empowered to make their impressions on the world. In addition to our 130-year commitment to public education, we have fortified our dedication to equitable academic excellence. MCLA has appeared on U.S. News & World Report's list of Top Ten Public Colleges for 10 consecutive years, earning the No. 6 spot on the list of Top Public Liberal Arts Schools in the nation for 2025, after earning the No. 7 spot the prior three years. The College's focus on affordable education and economic prosperity is reflected in additional 2025 U.S. News rankings: No. 5 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for liberal arts colleges in the state and No. 2 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for public liberal arts colleges in the country. These rankings measure how well schools graduate students who receive Federal Pell Grants. Learn more at www.mcla.edu Job Description: GENERAL STATEMENT OF DUTIES: The Facilities Manager is responsible for the planning, direction and supervision of all day-to-day activities related to second shift operations, custodial care, and maintenance of campus buildings and residence areas. This position requires a flexible work schedule that can include weekends. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: Reports to the Interim Assistant Director of Facilities Management SUPERVISION EXERCISED: Supervises classified employees assigned to related areas of the Facilities Department DETAILED STATEMENT OF DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Plan the second shift maintenance and custodial care of campus buildings and residence areas. Supervise, train, and evaluate all second shift custodial staff. Manage attendance records, time away approvals and overtime for all supervisees. Manage the purchasing and inventory control of equipment, furnishings, materials, and supplies required for the Operations and Maintenance area of Facilities Department. Provide weekly reports to the Interim Assistant Director of Facilities Department. Responsible for assuring timely communications with departments to give work status/updates. Develop and implement staff training and development programs for Maintainers. Prepare performance evaluations of assigned staff for Interim Assistant Director of Facilities review. Work with Interim Assistant Director of Facilities and Human Resources to address performance and disciplinary matters, referencing appropriate areas of the collective bargaining agreement. Develop and maintain standards of service in assigned work areas and provide a basis for evaluating employees and their work. Provide timely communications regarding work status updates to appropriate parties. Conduct daily walk-throughs and inspections of the campus-wide areas, including residence halls, academic, faculty and administrative buildings. Appropriately address concerns and issues observed. Respond to campus emergencies and critical incidents, as directed. Participate in the Department of Facilities Management administrator on-call schedule, as assigned. Ensure unit is in compliance with all federal, state and local laws and regulations, operating, environmental and safety procedures, and the College's policies and procedures including but not limited to HAZMAT and OSHA. Prioritize and distribute request (W.O.) and SchoolDude reports to facilities staff. Responsible for other duties as assigned. Requirements: Knowledge of and experience with facilities. Minimum of five years of experience in facilities management. Experience supervising in a collective bargaining environment preferred. Demonstrated knowledge and experience with federal and state laws and regulations regarding safety; OSHA, EPA, HAZMAT, etc. OSHA 10-Hour training and certificate preferred. Demonstrated ability to develop, promote and implement plans and proposals. Demonstrated ability to relate to others, and especially to manage, supervise and motivate staff. Demonstrated ability to express oneself professionally in written and oral communication. Proficient in the use of computers and database systems for providing assistance in facilities management; inventory control, work orders, preventive maintenance, building automation, word processing and other departmental functions. Experience on a residential campus or working within a residential environment preferred Additional Information: This is a full-time, permanent, benefited position within the APA bargaining union.  The annual salary for this position is $62,000 - $65,000 per year. This is a second shift position. Hours are Monday-Friday 3pm-11pm, with some weekends required. Employee Benefits: Health Insurance: MCLA offers a variety of HMO, POS, and PPO-type health insurance plans for eligible employees. Coverage is effective on the 1st of the month following the date of hire. Exceptions to employees hired on the 1st of the month, coverage is effective immediately. Retirement: The MA State Employee Retirement System provides eligible employees with a retirement pension following a 10-year vesting period. In lieu of the retirement pension, eligible employees may select the Optional Retirement Plan with a maximum 5% employer matching contribution. Tuition Waivers & Discounts: eligible employees, including spouses and dependent children, receive reduced tuition at MA state colleges, community colleges, and universities. Paid Time Off: employees receive 12 paid holidays and generous vacation, personal, and sick leave benefits. Until further notice, in response to the Presidential proclamation, issued on September 19, 2025, imposing a significant fee on the entry of individuals with new H-1B visas, this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. Should you need to request a reasonable accommodation for the application process, please email Brenda Stokes, Executive Director of Human Resources. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts is deeply committed to fostering a community of excellence, equity, diversity, and inclusion. We provide equal access to educational, co-curricular and employment opportunities for all applicants, students, and employees regardless of race, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, marital or parental status, veteran status, or membership in any other legally protected class. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any educational program or activity that they operate, which extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about Title IX, Equal Opportunity, or ADA/504 and other non-discrimination policies may be directed to MCLA's Interim Title IX and Equal Opportunity Coordinator, to the Assistant Secretary of the Department of Education Office for Civil Rights, or both. Lucas Morrill Interim Title IX and EO Coordinator 375 Church Street, North Adams, MA 01247 Telephone: (413) 662-5103 Titleix@mcla.edu U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights 33 Arch Street, 9th Floor Boston, MA 02119-1424 Telephone: (617) 289-0111; FAX: (617) 289-0150; TDD (877) 521-2172 OCR.Boston@ed.gov Application Instructions: Candidates are required to submit a resume, cover letter, online application and 3 professional references. To submit application materials, click the apply now button below. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Massachusetts college of liberal Arts - Main Campus 375 Church Street North Adams, MA 01247"
    },
    "http://mcla.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204035": {
      "title": "Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts \n\tJob Posting: Area Coordinator & Case Manager",
      "description": "Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts\nJob Posting: Area Coordinator & Case Manager Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts \n\tJob Posting: Area Coordinator & Case Manager Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Area Coordinator & Case Manager Category: Administrative Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Administrative &nbsp; Locations: North Adams, MA Posted: Aug 21, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204035 Share About Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts: At MCLA, we're here for all, and focused on each of our students. Classes are taught by educators who care deeply about teaching, and about seeing their students thrive on every level of their lives. In every way possible, the experience at MCLA is designed to elevate our students as individuals, leaders, and communicators, fully empowered to make their impressions on the world. In addition to our 130-year commitment to public education, we have fortified our dedication to equitable academic excellence. MCLA has appeared on U.S. News & World Report's list of Top Ten Public Colleges for 11 consecutive years, earning the No. 6 spot on the list of Top Public Liberal Arts Schools in the nation for 2026. The College's focus on affordable education and economic prosperity is reflected in additional 2026 U.S. News rankings: No. 6 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for liberal arts colleges in the state and No. 4 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for public liberal arts colleges in the country. These rankings measure how well schools graduate students who receive Federal Pell Grants. Learn more at www.mcla.edu Job Description: GENERAL STATEMENT OF DUTIES: The Area Coordinator (AC) & Case Manager is expected to be an active and visible member of our residence life staff with management and oversight of designated residence area(s). The AC will support resident student leadership opportunities through Residence Hall Association (RHA), National Residence Hall Honorary (NRHH) & other initiatives. The AC will participate in the administrative functions and efforts of Residence Life & Housing. As the supervisor of residential area(s), the AC will coordinate with other staff members in the Residence Life & Housing office on programs and events as needed. Further, they will be responsible for establishing and maintaining a living-learning atmosphere conducive to students' personal growth and academic achievement. Seen as a role model, facilitator, leader, and essential person in the development of an effective living-learning environment for student's experience. A successful individual will have the ability to work with a diverse population, able to adapt to change, and have knowledge of and commitment to maintaining a student development focus across campus. The individual will help shape the institution's vibrant living and learning community to help students build a sense of belonging to the College. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: Reports directly to the Assistant Director of Residence Life; indirectly to the Director of Residence Life. SUPERVISION EXERCISED: Directly supervises a number of para-professional student staff in residence areas. DETAILED STATEMENT OF DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Area Coordinator-50% Support the overall management of residence area(s) including but not limited to opening and closing the residence areas, key management, room changes, health & safety inspections, damage assessments and maintenance requests. This includes supporting the central office of Residence Life. Select, train, and evaluate all student staff assigned to the residence areas. Assistance in coordination and development of Resident Advisor (RA) In-Service Program. Select, train, evaluate, & supervise all Residence Area Security Monitors (RASMS) for Department. Contributes to experiential learning initiatives within the department and throughout campus to enhance the overall experience for students. Provide leadership and support to staff and residents in the planning and implementation of a wide range of educational, social and recreational activities that contribute to the personal growth and development of residence area members. Guide students toward responsible behavior in the residence area by communicating reasonable standards of behavior and by providing behavioral counseling or referral for students, as appropriate. Serve as an Advisor for RHA or NRHH, in collaboration with secondary Advisor as designated. Assist in management of departmental presence on social media platform accounts. Serve on the on-call rotation for emergency assistance and crisis intervention. Attend and actively participate in weekly staff meetings. Serve as department liaison for campus initiatives as designated by Director of Residence Life. Complete other duties and projects as assigned. This job description is subject to changes due to any organizational needs of the division. Serve as a conduct officer for lower-level violations of residence area policies. Case Manager-50% Support an identified case load of students by populations (examples: first-generation, student athletes, commuters, students with a GPA under 2.5, etc). Schedule appointments with students to assess risk and holistic needs, coordinate action plans, provide resources (on and off campus), non-clinical support and other follow-up as needed. Communicate, collaborate and follow through, as appropriate, with referral sources such as faculty, staff, campus partners and resources, external agencies, treatment providers, family members and emergency contacts in support of student well-being and persistence. Process and document student case information and notes to support data collection and uphold record keeping policies and procedures. Requirements: Required: Bachelor's degree required, Master's preferred Minimum of 1 to 3 years of relevant experience in Residence Life & Housing or education. Demonstrated ability to develop and maintain effective collaborative partnerships with other campus departments involved in creating a safe and engaging residential environment. Demonstrated ability to manage a variety of projects and responsibilities working both independently and collaboratively as necessary. Demonstrate flexibility, resiliency, creativity, leadership, and supervisory capabilities including demonstrating an active commitment to diversity and inclusive excellence. Ability to be flexible and adapt quickly to ever-changing needs of a residential campus. Preferred: Experience working with RHA's & NRHH. Knowledge and background working with NEACURH/NACURH. Additional Information: This is a full-time, permanent, benefited position within the APA bargaining union. Salary for this position is $44,000-$47,000 per year. This position includes on-campus housing and meal plan. Due to the nature of the position, ACs are expected to work outside of traditional business hours including participation in an on-call duty rotation. The duties of the Area Coordinator may vary due to the student population who resides in the area assigned. Employee Benefits: Health Insurance: MCLA offers a variety of HMO, POS, and PPO-type health insurance plans for eligible employees. Coverage is effective on the 1st of the month following the date of hire. Exceptions to employees hired on the 1st of the month, coverage is effective immediately. Retirement: The MA State Employee Retirement System provides eligible employees with a retirement pension following a 10-year vesting period. In lieu of the retirement pension, eligible employees may select the Optional Retirement Plan with a maximum 5% employer matching contribution. Tuition Waivers & Discounts: eligible employees, including spouses and dependent children, receive reduced tuition at MA state colleges, community colleges, and universities. Paid Time Off: employees receive 12 paid holidays and generous vacation, personal, and sick leave benefits. Until further notice, in response to the Presidential proclamation, issued on September 19, 2025, imposing a significant fee on the entry of individuals with new H-1B visas, this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. Should you need to request a reasonable accommodation for the application process, please email Brenda Stokes, Executive Director of Human Resources. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts is deeply committed to fostering a community of excellence, equity, diversity, and inclusion. We provide equal access to educational, co-curricular and employment opportunities for all applicants, students, and employees regardless of race, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, marital or parental status, veteran status, or membership in any other legally protected class. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any educational program or activity that they operate, which extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about Title IX, Equal Opportunity, or ADA/504 and other non-discrimination policies may be directed to MCLA's Interim Title IX and Equal Opportunity Coordinator, to the Assistant Secretary of the Department of Education Office for Civil Rights, or both. Lucas Morrill Interim Title IX and EO Coordinator 375 Church Street, North Adams, MA 01247 Telephone: (413) 662-5103 Titleix@mcla.edu U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights 33 Arch Street, 9th Floor Boston, MA 02119-1424 Telephone: (617) 289-0111; FAX: (617) 289-0150; TDD (877) 521-2172 OCR.Boston@ed.gov Application Instructions: Applicants are required to submit a resume, cover letter, online application and 3 professional references. Candidates should electronically submit an application materials by clicking on the APPLY NOW button below. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Massachusetts college of liberal Arts - Main Campus 375 Church Street North Adams, MA 01247"
    },
    "http://mcla.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203537": {
      "title": "Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts \n\tJob Posting: Nursing Simulation/Skills Lab Coordinator",
      "description": "Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts\nJob Posting: Nursing Simulation/Skills Lab Coordinator Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts \n\tJob Posting: Nursing Simulation/Skills Lab Coordinator Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Nursing Simulation/Skills Lab Coordinator Category: Administrative Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Academic Locations: North Adams, MA Posted: Aug 10, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 203537 Share About Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts: At MCLA, we're here for all, and focused on each of our students. Classes are taught by educators who care deeply about teaching, and about seeing their students thrive on every level of their lives. In every way possible, the experience at MCLA is designed to elevate our students as individuals, leaders, and communicators, fully empowered to make their impressions on the world. In addition to our 130-year commitment to public education, we have fortified our dedication to equitable academic excellence. MCLA has appeared on U.S. News & World Report's list of Top Ten Public Colleges for 11 consecutive years, earning the No. 6 spot on the list of Top Public Liberal Arts Schools in the nation for 2026. The College's focus on affordable education and economic prosperity is reflected in additional 2026 U.S. News rankings: No. 6 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for liberal arts colleges in the state and No. 4 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for public liberal arts colleges in the country. These rankings measure how well schools graduate students who receive Federal Pell Grants. Learn more at www.mcla.edu Job Description: GENERAL STATEMENT OF DUTIES: The Nursing Simulation/Skills Lab Coordinator works as part of the team in MCLA's Baccalaureate of Science in Nursing (BSN) Program and is an educational and technical expert who can develop, operate, maintain, troubleshoot, repair simulation and nursing skills lab equipment. The position works closely with nursing faculty members of the Baccalaureate of Science in Nursing (BSN) Program, supporting the Program and curriculum for the BSN major. This essential staff member is responsible for the overall day-to-day operations of the simulation/nursing skills lab focusing extensively on facilitating student learning outcomes associated with prescribed course and program outcomes, implementation of the nursing curriculum, program evaluation and improvement; supports the philosophy of nursing program and supports the mission of the College. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: Associate Dean of Nursing DETAILED STATEMENT OF DUTIES: Scheduling, planning, and running simulation and nursing skills events. Preparation, cleaning, and storage of all simulation and skills lab equipment and technology before, during, and after student learning events. Maintaining simulation and skills lab inventory and recommend purchasing to Associate Dean of Nursing. If Simulation Coordinator possesses a master's degree, teaching laboratory courses may be expected. Create an educational environment which fosters innovation, responsiveness, and accountability in the lab and clinical environment. Provide program-specific expertise and is actively engaged in relevant department initiatives. Serve as a professional role model for students in the lab and clinical environment. Requirements: Hold a current Massachusetts Registered Nurse license in good standing. Minimum of a bachelor's degree, master's degree preferred. Clinical experience in a specialty field; knowledge and experience in baccalaureate education preferred. Additional Information: This is a full-time, permanent, 10-month, benefited position within the APA bargaining union. Position starts in January 2027. Salary for this position is $56,000-$68,000 per year. Employee Benefits: Health Insurance: MCLA offers a variety of HMO, POS, and PPO-type health insurance plans for eligible employees. Coverage is effective on the 1st of the month following the date of hire. Exceptions to employees hired on the 1st of the month, coverage is effective immediately. Retirement: The MA State Employee Retirement System provides eligible employees with a retirement pension following a 10-year vesting period. In lieu of the retirement pension, eligible employees may select the Optional Retirement Plan with a maximum 5% employer matching contribution. Tuition Waivers & Discounts: eligible employees, including spouses and dependent children, receive reduced tuition at MA state colleges, community colleges, and universities. Paid Time Off: employees receive 12 paid holidays and generous vacation, personal, and sick leave benefits. Until further notice, in response to the Presidential proclamation, issued on September 19, 2025, imposing a significant fee on the entry of individuals with new H-1B visas, this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. Should you need to request a reasonable accommodation for the application process, please email Brenda Stokes, Executive Director of Human Resources. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts is deeply committed to fostering a community of excellence, equity, diversity, and inclusion. We provide equal access to educational, co-curricular and employment opportunities for all applicants, students, and employees regardless of race, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, marital or parental status, veteran status, or membership in any other legally protected class. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any educational program or activity that they operate, which extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about Title IX, Equal Opportunity, or ADA/504 and other non-discrimination policies may be directed to MCLA's Interim Title IX and Equal Opportunity Coordinator, to the Assistant Secretary of the Department of Education Office for Civil Rights, or both. Lucas Morrill Interim Title IX and EO Coordinator 375 Church Street, North Adams, MA 01247 Telephone: (413) 662-5103 Titleix@mcla.edu U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights 33 Arch Street, 9th Floor Boston, MA 02119-1424 Telephone: (617) 289-0111; FAX: (617) 289-0150; TDD (877) 521-2172 OCR.Boston@ed.gov Application Instructions: Candidates are required to submit a resume, cover letter, online application and 3 professional references. To submit application materials, click the apply now button below. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Massachusetts college of liberal Arts - Main Campus 375 Church Street North Adams, MA 01247"
