    "http://mcla.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205387": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty-Department of Graduate and Continuing Education",
      "description": "Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts\nJob Posting: Adjunct Faculty-Department of Graduate and Continuing Education Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Faculty-Department of Graduate and Continuing Education Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Faculty-Department of Graduate and Continuing Education Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Academic Locations: North Adams, MA Posted: Oct 1, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 205387 Share About Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts: At MCLA, we're here for all, and focused on each of our students. Classes are taught by educators who care deeply about teaching, and about seeing their students thrive on every level of their lives. In every way possible, the experience at MCLA is designed to elevate our students as individuals, leaders, and communicators, fully empowered to make their impressions on the world. In addition to our 132-year commitment to public education, we have fortified our dedication to equitable academic excellence. MCLA has appeared on U.S. News & World Report's list of Top Ten Public Colleges for 11 consecutive years, earning the No. 6 spot on the list of Top Public Liberal Arts Schools in the nation for 2026. The College's focus on affordable education and economic prosperity is reflected in additional 2026 U.S. News rankings: No. 6 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for liberal arts colleges in the state and No. 4 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for public liberal arts colleges in the country. These rankings measure how well schools graduate students who receive Federal Pell Grants. Learn more at www.mcla.edu Job Description: The Division of Graduate & Continuing Education (DGCE) at Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts (MCLA) is seeking applications for part-time, periodic instructional assignments in the education and business graduate degree programs as well as undergraduate courses in the summer and/or online during the fall or spring instructional period. Many course sections are scheduled as online/synchronous or hybrid with some courses delivered fully online in the MEd program while the MBA courses are delivered in a hybrid format at the Berkshire Innovation Center located in Pittsfield, Massachusetts. Requirements: Master's degree in appropriate field; Doctorate preferred Higher education teaching experience desirable Experience using Canvas or similar learning management system preferred Additional Information: This is a part time, temporary position within the MSCA union. The salary range for this position is $1,773.91-$2,047.09 per credit. Position starts on 1/20/2027. This position is for one semester with the opportunity for renewal. Until further notice, in response to the Presidential proclamation, issued on September 19, 2025, imposing a significant fee on the entry of individuals with new H-1B visas, this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. Should you need to request a reasonable accommodation for the application process, please email Brenda Stokes, Executive Director of Human Resources. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts is deeply committed to fostering a community of excellence, equity, diversity, and inclusion. We provide equal access to educational, co-curricular and employment opportunities for all applicants, students, and employees regardless of race, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, marital or parental status, veteran status, or membership in any other legally protected class. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any educational program or activity that they operate, which extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about Title IX, Equal Opportunity, or ADA/504 and other non-discrimination policies may be directed to MCLA's Interim Title IX and Equal Opportunity Coordinator, to the Assistant Secretary of the Department of Education Office for Civil Rights, or both. Lucas Morrill Interim Title IX and EO Coordinator 375 Church Street, North Adams, MA 01247 Telephone: (413) 662-5103 Titleix@mcla.edu U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights 33 Arch Street, 9th Floor Boston, MA 02119-1424 Telephone: (617) 289-0111; FAX: (617) 289-0150; TDD (877) 521-2172 OCR.Boston@ed.gov Application Instructions: Applicants are required to submit a resume, cover letter, online application, and 3 professional references to be considered for this position. Candidates should click the apply now button to submit application materials. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Massachusetts college of liberal Arts - Main Campus 375 Church Street North Adams, MA 01247"
    },
    "http://mcla.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205281": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty-Business Administration and Economics",
      "description": "Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts\nJob Posting: Adjunct Faculty-Business Administration and Economics Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Faculty-Business Administration and Economics Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Faculty-Business Administration and Economics Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Academic Locations: North Adams, MA Posted: Sep 28, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 205281 Share About Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts: At MCLA, we're here for all, and focused on each of our students. Classes are taught by educators who care deeply about teaching, and about seeing their students thrive on every level of their lives. In every way possible, the experience at MCLA is designed to elevate our students as individuals, leaders, and communicators, fully empowered to make their impressions on the world. In addition to our 132-year commitment to public education, we have fortified our dedication to equitable academic excellence. MCLA has appeared on U.S. News & World Report's list of Top Ten Public Colleges for 11 consecutive years, earning the No. 6 spot on the list of Top Public Liberal Arts Schools in the nation for 2026. The College's focus on affordable education and economic prosperity is reflected in additional 2026 U.S. News rankings: No. 6 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for liberal arts colleges in the state and No. 4 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for public liberal arts colleges in the country. These rankings measure how well schools graduate students who receive Federal Pell Grants. Learn more at www.mcla.edu Job Description: The Business Administration and Economics Department at MCLA seeks applications for part-time faculty in the areas of accounting, finance, and business law.  The program is designed to develop liberally educated professionals with the knowledge, perspectives, problem-solving abilities, and ethical values necessary for successful careers and responsible citizenship. Requirements: GENERAL REQUIREMENTS: Master's degree in a related field.  Doctorate preferred. Evidence of expertise, scholarly activity, or creative work appropriate to the discipline. Previous teaching experience at the college level is strongly preferred. Requirements to Teach Accounting Courses: Evidence of expertise, scholarly activity, or creative work appropriate to accounting. Prior college-level teach experience preferred, but not required CPA preferred Requirements to Teach Finance Courses: Evidence of expertise, scholarly activity, or creative work appropriate to finance. Demonstrated proficiency using Microsoft Excel and other relevant financial technologies Requirement to Teach Law Courses: Master's degree or higher in Business, Legal Studies, Accounting, Finance, or related field, or a Juris Doctor (J.D.) Knowledge of topics relevant to business, including contracts, agency, business organizations, employment law, regulatory compliance, ethics, and the legal environment of business Additional Information: This is a part time, temporary position within the MSCA union. Salary for this position is $1,166-$2,549 per credit. Pay is based on number of semesters previously taught. Position starts on 1/20/2027. Until further notice, in response to the Presidential proclamation, issued on September 19, 2025, imposing a significant fee on the entry of individuals with new H-1B visas, this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. Should you need to request a reasonable accommodation for the application process, please email Brenda Stokes, Executive Director of Human Resources. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts is deeply committed to fostering a community of excellence, equity, diversity, and inclusion. We provide equal access to educational, co-curricular and employment opportunities for all applicants, students, and employees regardless of race, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, marital or parental status, veteran status, or membership in any other legally protected class. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any educational program or activity that they operate, which extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about Title IX, Equal Opportunity, or ADA/504 and other non-discrimination policies may be directed to MCLA's Interim Title IX and Equal Opportunity Coordinator, to the Assistant Secretary of the Department of Education Office for Civil Rights, or both. Lucas Morrill Interim Title IX and EO Coordinator 375 Church Street, North Adams, MA 01247 Telephone: (413) 662-5103 Titleix@mcla.edu U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights 33 Arch Street, 9th Floor Boston, MA 02119-1424 Telephone: (617) 289-0111; FAX: (617) 289-0150; TDD (877) 521-2172 OCR.Boston@ed.gov Application Instructions: Applicants are required to submit a resume, cover letter, online application, and 3 professional references to be considered for this position. Candidates should click the apply now button to submit application materials. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Massachusetts college of liberal Arts - Main Campus 375 Church Street North Adams, MA 01247"
