    "http://mcla.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203699": {
      "title": "Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts \n\tJob Posting: Campus Police Officer I",
      "description": "Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts\nJob Posting: Campus Police Officer I Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts \n\tJob Posting: Campus Police Officer I Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Campus Police Officer I Category: Other Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Miscellaneous &nbsp; Locations: North Adams, MA Posted: Aug 13, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 203699 Share About Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts: At MCLA, we're here for all, and focused on each, of our students. Classes are taught by educators who care deeply about teaching, and about seeing their students thrive on every level of their lives. In every way possible, the experience at MCLA is designed to elevate our students as individuals, leaders, and communicators, fully empowered to make their impressions on the world. In addition to our 130-year commitment to public education, we have fortified our dedication to equitable academic excellence. MCLA has appeared on U.S. News & World Report's list of Top Ten Public Colleges for 10 consecutive years, earning the No. 6 spot on the list of Top Public Liberal Arts Schools in the nation for 2025, after earning the No. 7 spot the prior three years. The College's focus on affordable education and economic prosperity is reflected in additional 2025 U.S. News rankings: No. 5 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for liberal arts colleges in the state and No. 2 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for public liberal arts colleges in the country. These rankings measure how well schools graduate students who receive Federal Pell Grants. Learn more at www.mcla.edu Job Description: The Department of Public Safety/Campus Police at Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts (MCLA) invites applications for a Campus Police Officer I.  This is an armed position, Officer will patrol the campus buildings, grounds, and areas adjacent to the College, enforcing state and federal laws and MCLA rules and regulations.  This Officer will also ensure the safety, security and well-being of the College community through: investigating crimes and other incidents; restraining and/or arresting suspects when necessary; completing crime and incident reports; providing assistance to courts in prosecution cases; and performing other related work in accordance with campus needs. Requirements: Eligibility for appointment as a Massachusetts Special State Police Officer under Massachusetts General Law, Chapter 22C, Section 63 and must obtain Special State Police Powers from the Massachusetts State Police Must have graduated from a Massachusetts Special State Police Officer (SSPO) Academy OR Must have graduated from the Massachusetts Municipal Police Training Committee (MPTC) full-time Police Academy or other full-time reciprocal Police Academy If the candidate is not Police Academy trained, that candidate must be physically fit and able to successfully complete a full-time MPTC or SSPO training academy, to include all perquisites (which includes physical endurance testing). Failure to meet the entrance requirements or to successfully complete the course of training shall result in dismissal or, for lateral appointment within the bargaining unit, return to previously held position in accordance with the AFSCME Agreement. Must be able to pass the following pre-employment examinations: fit-for-duty physical and psychological assessments under the auspices of the Campus Police Department, as well as a thorough background check to include Criminal Offender Records Information Must have a criminal history free of ANY felony convictions Must have and retain a valid driver's license Must have or be able to obtain and retain a Massachusetts license to carry a firearm Must be able to stand and or walk for prolonged periods of time; while wearing issued and approved equipment (duty belt, protective body armor etc.). Ability to lift heavy objects or persons and possess physical stamina and endurance Must be able to work with diverse populations and have the ability to deal with young adults, faculty, and staff in a multicultural, multiracial environment Must possess excellent written and oral communication skills Ability to obtain a CPR/First Responder certification and training in the operation of Automated External Defibrillator Ability to successfully complete initial and annual firearms qualification training Ability to successfully complete annual in-service training requirements Computer literacy in the department's law enforcement technology preferred, including: word processing, LEAPS, ID equipment, various alarm systems/computers, and other security-related software Ability to obtain certification as a Law Enforcement Administration System Computer Operator Ability to complete Incident Command System training A basic knowledge and understanding of police procedures and how those procedures are adapted to an educational community, preferred Ability to work varied work schedules and shifts based on assignment and the needs of the Department/College Must successfully complete the required Field Training Officer Program Additional Information: The shift for this position is Midnight-8am Sunday-Monday and Thursday-Saturday with Tuesday and Wednesday off. This is a full-time, benefit-eligible, (Grade 16, Step 1) position in the AFSCME bargaining union.  Biweekly salary is $2,268.91. Weekend and shift differential eligible. Preference may be given to applicants who have graduated from a full-time Massachusetts Police Academy. Employee Benefits: Health Insurance: MCLA offers a variety of HMO, POS, and PPO-type health insurance plans for eligible employees. Coverage is effective on the 1st of the month following the date of hire. Exceptions to employees hired on the 1st of the month, coverage is effective immediately. Retirement: The MA State Employee Retirement System provides eligible employees with a retirement pension following a 10-year vesting period. In lieu of the retirement pension, eligible employees may select the Optional Retirement Plan with a maximum 5% employer matching contribution. Tuition Waivers & Discounts: eligible employees, including spouses and dependent children, receive reduced tuition at MA state colleges, community colleges, and universities. Paid Time Off: employees receive 12 paid holidays and generous vacation, personal, and sick leave benefits. Until further notice, in response to the Presidential proclamation, issued on September 19, 2025, imposing a significant fee on the entry of individuals with new H-1B visas, this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. Should you need to request a reasonable accommodation for the application process, please email Brenda Stokes, Executive Director of Human Resources. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts is deeply committed to fostering a community of excellence, equity, diversity, and inclusion. We provide equal access to educational, co-curricular and employment opportunities for all applicants, students, and employees regardless of race, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, marital or parental status, veteran status, or membership in any other legally protected class. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any educational program or activity that they operate, which extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about Title IX, Equal Opportunity, or ADA/504 and other non-discrimination policies may be directed to MCLA's Interim Title IX and Equal Opportunity Coordinator, to the Assistant Secretary of the Department of Education Office for Civil Rights, or both. Lucas Morrill Interim Title IX and EO Coordinator 375 Church Street, North Adams, MA 01247 Telephone: (413) 662-5103 Titleix@mcla.edu U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights 33 Arch Street, 9th Floor Boston, MA 02119-1424 Telephone: (617) 289-0111; FAX: (617) 289-0150; TDD (877) 521-2172 OCR.Boston@ed.gov Application Instructions: Applicants are required to submit a resume, cover letter, online application and 3 professional references. Candidates can submit application materials by clicking on the APPLY NOW button below. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Massachusetts college of liberal Arts - Main Campus 375 Church Street North Adams, MA 01247"
    },
    "http://mcla.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=200067": {
      "title": "Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts \n\tJob Posting: Part Time - Assistant Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts\nJob Posting: Part Time - Assistant Athletic Trainer Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts \n\tJob Posting: Part Time - Assistant Athletic Trainer Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Part Time - Assistant Athletic Trainer Category: Support Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: North Adams, MA Posted: May 1, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 200067 Share About Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts: At MCLA, we're here for all, and focused on each of our students. Classes are taught by educators who care deeply about teaching, and about seeing their students thrive on every level of their lives. In every way possible, the experience at MCLA is designed to elevate our students as individuals, leaders, and communicators, fully empowered to make their impressions on the world. In addition to our 130-year commitment to public education, we have fortified our dedication to equitable academic excellence. MCLA has appeared on U.S. News & World Report's list of Top Ten Public Colleges for 11 consecutive years, earning the No. 6 spot on the list of Top Public Liberal Arts Schools in the nation for 2026. The College's focus on affordable education and economic prosperity is reflected in additional 2026 U.S. News rankings: No. 6 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for liberal arts colleges in the state and No. 4 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for public liberal arts colleges in the country. These rankings measure how well schools graduate students who receive Federal Pell Grants. Learn more at www.mcla.edu Job Description: Detailed Statement of Duties: Assistant Athletic Trainer Care for and provide treatment, assessment, rehabilitation, prevention and referral for student-athlete injuries. Maintain and input medical files and notes for student-athletes through SportsWare (EMR). Maintain communication with student-athletes, coaches, and medical staff regarding the care and prevention of athletic injuries Provide athletic training coverage for practices and competitions as appointed by the Director of Athletics and in consultation from the Head Athletic Trainer.  Practice and game coverage will include some nights, weekends, and holidays. Assist with preseason clearances and concussion testing for student-athletes. Administrative Responsibilities Support mission and vision of athletic department Complete all department, College, and conference trainings Conform to the highest standards of professional conduct regarding compliance with department, institutional and conference policies and procedures and adhere to the rules and regulations of athletic governance organizations of which the institution is a member Contribute to the maintenance of good working relationships with all staff, student-athletes, and external constituents through (a) a positive and constructive approach to all tasks, (b) respect for the competencies of others, and (c) appropriate conflict resolution behavior Any staff member who is found in violation of NCAA regulations shall be subject to disciplinary or corrective action set forth in the provisions of the NCAA enforcement procedure and in accordance with the terms of any applicable collective bargaining agreement, and a staff member may be suspended without pay or terminated if the coach is found to be involved in deliberate and serious violations of NCAA regulations. Requirements: Bachelor's degree required, Master's preferred National Athletic Trainers Association (N.A.T.A.) Certifications Massachusetts State License (Board of Registration of Allied Health Professions) or Eligible One to three years of Collegiate Athletic Training or related experience preferred An awareness of higher education principles, practices, and procedures Strong interpersonal skills Ability to express self in written and oral communication Ability to work effectively with professional, non-professional, and student personnel Excellent organizational skills and demonstrated attention to detail Ability to demonstrate appropriate level of initiative Additional Information: MCLA is currently hiring for two Assistant Athletic Trainers These are part-time, temporary, non-benefitted positions starting on 8/10/26 and going through 10/18/26. The Assistant Athletic Trainer will be working up to 18.5 hours per week. Salary for this position is $32.25/hour. Until further notice, in response to the Presidential proclamation, issued on September 19, 2025, imposing a significant fee on the entry of individuals with new H-1B visas, this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. Should you need to request a reasonable accommodation for the application process, please email Brenda Stokes, Executive Director of Human Resources. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts is deeply committed to fostering a community of excellence, equity, diversity, and inclusion. We provide equal access to educational, co-curricular and employment opportunities for all applicants, students, and employees regardless of race, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, marital or parental status, veteran status, or membership in any other legally protected class. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any educational program or activity that they operate, which extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about Title IX, Equal Opportunity, or ADA/504 and other non-discrimination policies may be directed to MCLA's Interim Title IX and Equal Opportunity Coordinator, to the Assistant Secretary of the Department of Education Office for Civil Rights, or both. Lucas Morrill Interim Title IX and EO Coordinator 375 Church Street, North Adams, MA 01247 Telephone: (413) 662-5103 Titleix@mcla.edu U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights 33 Arch Street, 9th Floor Boston, MA 02119-1424 Telephone: (617) 289-0111; FAX: (617) 289-0150; TDD (877) 521-2172 OCR.Boston@ed.gov Application Instructions: Applicants should electronically submit an application by clicking on the APPLY NOW button below. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Massachusetts college of liberal Arts - Main Campus 375 Church Street North Adams, MA 01247"
    },
    "http://mcla.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205729": {
      "title": "Student Financial Services Operations Clerk VI",
      "description": "Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts\nJob Posting: Student Financial Services Operations Clerk VI Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts \n\tJob Posting: Student Financial Services Operations Clerk VI Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Student Financial Services Operations Clerk VI Category: Administrative Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Academic Locations: North Adams, MA Posted: Oct 13, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 205729 Share About Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts: At MCLA, we're here for all, and focused on each of our students. Classes are taught by educators who care deeply about teaching, and about seeing their students thrive on every level of their lives. In every way possible, the experience at MCLA is designed to elevate our students as individuals, leaders, and communicators, fully empowered to make their impressions on the world. In addition to our 132-year commitment to public education, we have fortified our dedication to equitable academic excellence. MCLA has appeared on U.S. News & World Report's list of Top Ten Public Colleges for 11 consecutive years, earning the No. 6 spot on the list of Top Public Liberal Arts Schools in the nation for 2026. The College's focus on affordable education and economic prosperity is reflected in additional 2026 U.S. News rankings: No. 6 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for liberal arts colleges in the state and No. 4 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for public liberal arts colleges in the country. These rankings measure how well schools graduate students who receive Federal Pell Grants. Learn more at www.mcla.edu Job Description: GENERAL STATEMENT OF DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Operating under the direct supervision of the Assistant Director and general strategic oversight and direction of the Executive Director of Student Financial Services, the SFS Operations Clerk handles high-volume administrative support, routine file exchanges, C-code/verification processing, state grant/scholarship files, and frontline customer service for students and families. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: Direct supervision from the Assistant Director of Student Financial Services with executive oversight by the Executive Director of Student Financial Services SUPERVISION EXERCISED: Supervision of work-study student(s) as assigned. DETAILED STATEMENT OF DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITES: State Grants & Third-Party Sponsorships: Assist with the management and disbursement of state grant and scholarship files (OSFA, VSAC, out-of-state agencies) in Banner and state portals. Process third-party sponsorships, outside scholarships, and complete verification forms for social service agencies. Scholarship Administration & Systems Leadership: Serve as the primary administrator for the AwardSpring scholarship management system and manage the administration of institutional and donor-funded scholarship programs, including award processing, eligibility review, coordination with scholarship committees, annual scholarship renewals, and reconciliation of scholarship funds. Frontline Student & Family Counseling: Serve as a preliminary point of contact for financial aid and student account inquiries received by phone, email, and front desk walk-ins, in coordination with the Clerk V in Student Financial Services. Counsel students and parents on financial aid application processes, billing schedules, and available funding options. Transactional & Administrative Support: Process award cancellations due to enrollment status changes; assist with preparation of consortium agreements. Maintain office supply inventory, form updates, routine mailings, and general file maintenance. Supervision Support: Assist with hiring, scheduling, and daily workflow oversight of student work-study employees in the SFS office. Assist the Assistant Director and Executive Director with non-director level duties as assigned. Requirements: QUALIFICATIONS: Education & Experience: Associate's degree preferred. 3+ years of administrative or customer service experience in a higher education financial aid or student financial services environment; experience administering scholarships. Technical Skills: Working knowledge of Student Information Systems (Ellucian Banner preferred), EDConnect, state portals (OSFA/VSAC), and Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, Outlook). Core Competencies: Strong organizational skills and detail-oriented processing; ability to communicate financial information clearly and empathetically to students and parents; strong customer service skills. Additional Information: This is a full-time, permanent, benefited position within the AFSCME bargaining union. Salary for this position is $2,268.91 bi-weekly. Employee Benefits: Health Insurance: MCLA offers a variety of HMO, POS, and PPO-type health insurance plans for eligible employees. Coverage is effective on the 1st of the month following the date of hire. Exceptions to employees hired on the 1st of the month, coverage is effective immediately. Retirement: The MA State Employee Retirement System provides eligible employees with a retirement pension following a 10-year vesting period. In lieu of the retirement pension, eligible employees may select the Optional Retirement Plan with a maximum 5% employer matching contribution. Tuition Waivers & Discounts: eligible employees, including spouses and dependent children, receive reduced tuition at MA state colleges, community colleges, and universities. Paid Time Off: employees receive 12 paid holidays and generous vacation, personal, and sick leave benefits. Until further notice, in response to the Presidential proclamation, issued on September 19, 2025, imposing a significant fee on the entry of individuals with new H-1B visas, this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. Should you need to request a reasonable accommodation for the application process, please email Brenda Stokes, Executive Director of Human Resources. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts is deeply committed to fostering a community of excellence, equity, diversity, and inclusion. We provide equal access to educational, co-curricular and employment opportunities for all applicants, students, and employees regardless of race, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, marital or parental status, veteran status, or membership in any other legally protected class. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any educational program or activity that they operate, which extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about Title IX, Equal Opportunity, or ADA/504 and other non-discrimination policies may be directed to MCLA's Interim Title IX and Equal Opportunity Coordinator, to the Assistant Secretary of the Department of Education Office for Civil Rights, or both. Lucas Morrill Interim Title IX and EO Coordinator 375 Church Street, North Adams, MA 01247 Telephone: (413) 662-5103 Titleix@mcla.edu U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights 33 Arch Street, 9th Floor Boston, MA 02119-1424 Telephone: (617) 289-0111; FAX: (617) 289-0150; TDD (877) 521-2172 OCR.Boston@ed.gov Application Instructions: Applicants are required to submit a resume, cover letter, online application and 3 professional references. Candidates should electronically submit an application materials by clicking on the APPLY NOW button below. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Massachusetts college of liberal Arts - Main Campus 375 Church Street North Adams, MA 01247"
    },
    "http://mcla.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205713": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Student Financial Services",
      "description": "Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts\nJob Posting: Assistant Director of Student Financial Services Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Director of Student Financial Services Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Director of Student Financial Services Category: Administrative Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Administrative &nbsp; Locations: North Adams, MA Posted: Oct 13, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 205713 Share About Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts: At MCLA, we're here for all, and focused on each of our students. Classes are taught by educators who care deeply about teaching, and about seeing their students thrive on every level of their lives. In every way possible, the experience at MCLA is designed to elevate our students as individuals, leaders, and communicators, fully empowered to make their impressions on the world. In addition to our 132-year commitment to public education, we have fortified our dedication to equitable academic excellence. MCLA has appeared on U.S. News & World Report's list of Top Ten Public Colleges for 11 consecutive years, earning the No. 6 spot on the list of Top Public Liberal Arts Schools in the nation for 2026. The College's focus on affordable education and economic prosperity is reflected in additional 2026 U.S. News rankings: No. 6 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for liberal arts colleges in the state and No. 4 for Top Performer on Social Mobility for public liberal arts colleges in the country. These rankings measure how well schools graduate students who receive Federal Pell Grants. Learn more at www.mcla.edu Job Description: GENERAL STATEMENT OF DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: The Assistant Director exercises substantial independent judgment while operating under the strategic direction of the Executive Director. The Assistant Director manages all institutional loan programs (federal, private, and state) and serves as an administrative officer within the SFS office. The Assistant Director oversees Satisfactory Academic Progress (SAP), assists with appeals and Special Circumstance professional judgment evaluations, provides oversight of institutional scholarship programs, and conducts financial aid file reviews upon request by the Executive Director. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: Executive Director of Student Financial Services SUPERVISION EXERCISED: Student Financial Services Clerks and Student Work-Study Employees DETAILED STATEMENT OF DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITES: EDConnect & Data Systems File Exchanges: Execute daily import and export file exchanges between EDConnect and Banner. Monitor and troubleshoot routine batch transmission issues, origination flags, and record errors. Comprehensive Loan Program Management: Direct and manage the origination, certification, processing, and disbursement of all Federal Direct Student Loans (Subsidized, Unsubsidized, Parent/Graduate PLUS), private/alternative student loans, and state loan programs (including VSAC and out-of-state loan processing). Interface with COD, lender portals, and ELM; manage loan revisions, cancellations, transfer student default/grant overpayment checks via NSLDS, and exit counseling compliance summaries. Return of Title IV Funds: Calculate and process Return of Title IV Funds (R2T4) for withdrawn students in accordance with federal regulations and institutional policies. Coordinate with Student Accounts to ensure timely return of funds and student notification. Packaging: Package and repackage student financial aid awards in accordance with federal, state, and institutional requirements. Scholarship Program Oversight: Provide supervisory oversight of the SFS Operations Clerk's administration of institutional and donor-funded scholarship programs, including award processing, eligibility review, scholarship committee coordination, annual renewals, and reconciliation of scholarship funds. Enrollment Support: Collaborate with Admissions, Enrollment Management, Student Success, and Academic Affairs to support recruitment, retention, persistence, and affordability initiatives. Professional Judgment & Special Circumstances: On an ad hoc basis,  review Special Circumstance appeals, income adjustments, and dependency overrides using professional judgment in strict accordance with federal Title IV regulations and institutional standards, referring unprecedented policy cases to the Executive Director. Satisfactory Academic Progress (SAP) Administration: Monitor academic progress for all aid applicants in accordance with federal regulations and college policy. Manage the formal SAP appeal process, coordinate appeal committees, collaborate with academic affairs on academic warning/attendance data, and counsel students on aid restoration. Verification Processing & C-Code Clearance: Process standard federal/institutional verification files and clear C-code ISIR flags (e.g., citizenship, Selective Service, NSLDS flags). Collect required tax forms and household documentation to clear files for aid disbursement. Office Supervision & Operational Coordination: Assist in the direct day-to-day office workflow and supervise, evaluate, and mentor SFS staff and student work-study employees under the oversight of the Executive Director. Coordinate activity between Financial Aid and Student Accounts. Reconciliations: Under the oversight of the Executive Director, oversee program reconciliations for institutional, state, and federal aid programs. Assist the Executive Director with statistical/financial reporting, audit preparation, policy enforcement, and annual publication updates. Advanced Counseling & Events: Provide elevated financial aid and billing counseling for complex student cases, study abroad/consortium agreements, and special populations. Present at Admissions open houses, financial aid nights, and orientation events. Requirements: QULIFICATIONS: Education & Experience: Bachelor's degree required and Master's degree preferred.  5+ years of progressive experience in higher education financial aid administration, with specific experience in federal Direct Loan management and professional staff supervision. Experience administering scholarships. Experience with SAP and Professional Judgment. Experience in public higher education preferred. Technical Expertise: Proficiency with Student Information Systems (Ellucian Banner preferred), Department of Education portals (COD, NSLDS), scholarship management software (AwardSpring), and Microsoft Office Suite. Core Competencies: In-depth understanding of Title IV regulations and professional judgment guidelines; regulatory interpretation; strong analytical and quantitative skills; project management; data analysis; conflict resolution; exceptional interpersonal communication; presentation and public speaking. Additional Information: This is a full time, permanent, benefited position within the APA bargaining union. Salary for this position is $100,000-$110,000 per year. Employee Benefits: Health Insurance: MCLA offers a variety of HMO, POS, and PPO-type health insurance plans for eligible employees. Coverage is effective on the 1st of the month following the date of hire. Exceptions to employees hired on the 1st of the month, coverage is effective immediately. Retirement: The MA State Employee Retirement System provides eligible employees with a retirement pension following a 10-year vesting period. In lieu of the retirement pension, eligible employees may select the Optional Retirement Plan with a maximum 5% employer matching contribution. Tuition Waivers & Discounts: eligible employees, including spouses and dependent children, receive reduced tuition at MA state colleges, community colleges, and universities. Paid Time off: employees receive 12 paid holidays and generous vacation, personal, and sick leave benefits. Until further notice, in response to the Presidential proclamation, issued on September 19, 2025, imposing a significant fee on the entry of individuals with new H-1B visas, this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. Should you need to request a reasonable accommodation for the application process, please email Brenda Stokes, Executive Director of Human Resources. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts is deeply committed to fostering a community of excellence, equity, diversity, and inclusion. We provide equal access to educational, co-curricular and employment opportunities for all applicants, students, and employees regardless of race, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, marital or parental status, veteran status, or membership in any other legally protected class. Massachusetts College of Liberal Arts does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any educational program or activity that they operate, which extends to admission and employment. Inquiries about Title IX, Equal Opportunity, or ADA/504 and other non-discrimination policies may be directed to MCLA's Interim Title IX and Equal Opportunity Coordinator, to the Assistant Secretary of the Department of Education Office for Civil Rights, or both. Lucas Morrill Interim Title IX and EO Coordinator 375 Church Street, North Adams, MA 01247 Telephone: (413) 662-5103 Titleix@mcla.edu U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights 33 Arch Street, 9th Floor Boston, MA 02119-1424 Telephone: (617) 289-0111; FAX: (617) 289-0150; TDD (877) 521-2172 OCR.Boston@ed.gov Application Instructions: Applicants are required to submit a resume, cover letter, online application and 3 professional references. Candidates should electronically submit an application materials by clicking on the APPLY NOW button below. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Massachusetts college of liberal Arts - Main Campus 375 Church Street North Adams, MA 01247"
